&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Sweet James Accident Attorneys is a rapidly growing, AI-powered personal injury firm based in Orange County, CA. In less than a decade, we&#39;ve built a nationally recognized brand and a proprietary AI and automation stack that make us one of the largest and most efficient providers of legal services in the country. Our growth runs on a culture of excellence, compassion, and results: Our team is committed to exceptional client experience and to supporting one another in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. We invest in our people, encourage professional growth, and provide meaningful opportunities to build rewarding careers while making a real impact in our clients&#39; lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Scale: &lt;/strong&gt;$23.00–$28.00 per hour (base pay)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;In addition to base pay, this role is eligible to participate in a performance-based bonus program that rewards strong results, subject to program terms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work arrangement: &lt;/strong&gt;On-site&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Schedule&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work hours will encompass varying shift options, on-site at our Newport Beach office. You must be available to work weekends [on rotation] and potential holidays. Schedules are set in advance, but may range from start times as early as 7am to as late as 11am.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the first point of contact for accident victims calling Sweet James.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Listen with empathy and urgency, reassuring clients in moments of pain and confusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidently explain our services and help clients take the step of signing with our firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualify potential cases quickly and accurately, ensuring we’re aligned to deliver results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive performance while maintaining the highest standards of care.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take initiative in every interaction, leading conversations, overcoming objections, and closing retainers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with both empathy and command, balancing compassion with persistence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with legal and client service teams to ensure smooth case handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solid work ethic and positive attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work well under pressure while maintaining a positive attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in customer service, sales or other related fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available to work after hours and occasional weekends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bilingual (Spanish) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sales background with a proven track record of meeting and exceeding goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive, ambitious, and results-driven personality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of emotional intelligence with the ability to show genuine empathy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and active listening skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform under pressure and thrive in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter who takes initiative and leads conversations with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Goal-oriented mindset with the discipline to execute consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benefits package: medical, dental, vision, and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FSA or HSA option, depending on the selected medical plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with 2% match after 90 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid time off (PTO) policy and paid holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing mentorship, leadership support, and professional development and career advancement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sweet James, we don&#39;t just offer jobs - we build careers. If you&#39;re ready to join a firm that values excellence with an unwavering passion for life changing results, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Sweet James is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applicants of every background and do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot; data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;We will consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records in accordance with the California Fair Chance Act and applicable local law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Stay safe: We will never ask for payment or banking information during the hiring process.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;x_elementToProof&quot;&gt;Questions? Contact &amp;nbsp;&lt;a id=&quot;OWA43989ecb-0405-255c-58e0-937c1bb2588c&quot; class=&quot;x_OWAAutoLink&quot; href=&quot;mailto:careers@sweetjames.com&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;d7bf98f9-487a-41a0-a2d8-2222e1322344&quot; data-linkindex=&quot;0&quot;&gt;careers@sweetjames.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Sweet James Accident Attorneys is a rapidly growing, AI-powered personal injury firm based in Orange County, CA. In less than a decade, we&#39;ve built a nationally recognized brand and a proprietary AI and automation stack that make us one of the largest and most efficient providers of legal services in the country. Our growth runs on a culture of excellence, compassion, and results: Our team is committed to exceptional client experience and to supporting one another in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. We invest in our people, encourage professional growth, and provide meaningful opportunities to build rewarding careers while making a real impact in our clients&#39; lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Scale: &lt;/strong&gt;$160,000–$200,000 per year (base pay)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work arrangement: &lt;/strong&gt;On-site&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is our first dedicated client experience leadership hire. Our clients come to us at one of the hardest moments of their lives, and their case can run for many months across intake, treatment, negotiation, settlement, and disbursement. Each stage is handled by a team built for that stage, resulting in a fragmented client experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director of Client Success, you&#39;ll own that journey. Your first mandate is diagnostic: Spend your first weeks mapping the client journey as clients actually experience it, analyzing the data behind client attrition and complaints, and interviewing employees and current and former clients to establish a baseline, name the gaps, and recommend what to do about them. Your second mandate is to build: Rework our client-facing roles (e.g., our settlement concierge team), either by rebuilding what exists or standing up and leading new teams from scratch, and design the operating model, metrics, and escalation paths that keep clients informed and cared for from the day they retain us to the day they receive their settlement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Managing Partner of Pre-Litigation and work across attorneys, case management, settlement, and accounting teams, as well as our offices outside California. You will have the mandate to change how client-facing work is organized and be held accountable for the results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose the baseline: Map the end-to-end client journey, analyze attrition, complaint, and review data, and interview staff and current and former clients to produce a baseline assessment of our client experience, its gaps, and prioritized recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the operating model: Define the client experience strategy and the roles, handoffs, service standards, and escalation paths that deliver it at every stage of the case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the teams: Rebuild existing client-facing teams (e.g., settlement concierge) or stand up new ones (e.g., a client success function that monitors the client relationship across the journey and intervenes early), including hiring, training, and day-to-day leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the metrics: Define the client experience metrics that matter (e.g., client satisfaction, complaint rate, response times, attrition), build the reporting behind them, and use the results to pilot, measure, and iterate on what you have built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the escalation system: Create mechanisms that surface unhappy clients before they leave (e.g., early-warning signals drawn from case and communication data, proactive check-ins at high-risk stages) and routing that ensures every escalation is captured, assigned to the right person, and resolved on time, with visibility into what was handled and what was not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across the firm: Work with attorneys, case management, settlement, accounting, and regional office leaders so client-facing changes fit how cases are actually worked, and ensure client communications operate within the professional-responsibility rules that govern a law firm, under attorney guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Required&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years building and leading customer success, customer experience, or customer service teams, including direct management of people and managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record as a builder: You have stood up a team or function from scratch or rebuilt one that was underperforming, and can describe what you inherited, what you changed, and what happened.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics orientation: You have defined customer experience metrics, built the reporting behind them, and managed teams against them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operating model experience: You have designed and refined roles, processes, service standards, and escalation paths for a customer-facing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on with escalations: You have personally managed high-stakes customer escalations and can describe how you resolved them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independence: You can define a strategy from an ambiguous mandate, prioritize ruthlessly, and execute with limited direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in customer experience best practices (e.g., journey mapping, voice-of-customer programs, service recovery, tiered support models).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Preferred&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a start-up or rapidly scaling environment where you built the function while the business grew around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a regulated or professional-services setting (e.g., legal, healthcare, financial services) where customer communications carry compliance constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience serving consumers in high-stress, high-stakes situations rather than business-to-business accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working directly in customer relationship management or case-management data (e.g., Salesforce) to answer your own questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who succeeds here&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a builder who is comfortable being handed a problem rather than a plan. You would rather spend a few weeks understanding how clients actually experience us than start reorganizing on day one, and once you have the picture, you move fast, iterate quickly, and scale what works. You hold yourself and your teams to measurable outcomes and treat a client&#39;s worst day as the moment that matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are also comfortable operating inside a law firm: Attorneys own the legal advice, and you own the experience around it. You know how to earn the trust of people who have run their teams a certain way for years, and you can change how work gets done without leaving clients confused about who is looking after them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benefits package: medical, dental, vision, and life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FSA or HSA option, depending on the selected medical plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with 2% match after 90 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid time off (PTO) policy and paid holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing mentorship, leadership support, and professional development and career advancement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sweet James, we don&#39;t just offer jobs - we build careers. If you&#39;re ready to join a firm that values excellence with an unwavering passion for life changing results, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
