&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sweet James is seeking a Manager of Strategy &amp;amp; Operations to work alongside the Chief of Staff on the highest-priority problems facing the firm. This is an execution seat, not an advisory one: you will own initiatives from diagnosis through implementation and be measured on what changes in the business, not on the quality of the recommendation. Assignments rotate across contact center and operational performance, organizational design, technology and product initiatives, and the growth priorities the executive team needs solved, with a path to owning a function or domain outright as the firm scales. The work suits a generalist equally comfortable building the model, running the project, and persuading a function to change how it works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose performance: Identify where the business is underperforming, structure the problem, and define what success looks like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the analysis: Construct the models, size the opportunities, and build the business cases that inform executive decisions; pull and interrogate your own data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver the result: Run the implementation yourself, through to the operating change and the measured outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move work across functions: Drive progress where you hold no formal authority, earning credibility with operators by understanding their work before changing it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Institutionalize what works: Convert delivered initiatives into repeatable systems and hand them to the function that will own them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance technology and product priorities: Partner with engineering and product leadership on prioritization, roadmap, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate to the executive team: Translate analysis into crisp recommendations for the Chief of Staff, the CEO, and the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
